\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Quantitative comparison on the Dense Layout test set~\cite  {xiang2025instanceassemble} ($5{,}000$ images; mean $8.3$ objects/image). Baselines use five references (UNO/XVerse cannot run beyond this on one H100); the $N{>}5$ RefCompose row uses additional references. Higher is better. \textbf  {Bold} = best overall; improvement row compares RefCompose ($N{>}5$) against the strongest reference-image baseline per metric.}}{10}{table.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
